      { title: 'Use it in a few calm routines', do: 'Practice near a familiar doorway or before setting down a toy, away from traffic and crowding.', watch: 'Notice whether your dog can sit briefly and rise freely without discomfort.', reward: 'Reward the sit, then use the release cue so the dog knows the pause has ended.', repeat: 'If a greeting or environment makes sitting difficult, increase space and let the dog stand.', ready: 'Add a new room or mild distraction only when the dog remains comfortable.' }
